DevList: build the devicelist.json path inside main()

kUSBDescriptorPath was a global initialized from tacConfigRoot(), which reads
kAppName, a global in another translation unit (ConsoleApplicationEnhancements.cpp).
C++ does not order static initialization across translation units, so kAppName
could still be empty, the installed path was missed, and DevList fell back to
../../../../configurations/devicelist.json.

diff --git a/src/applications/devlist/main.cpp b/src/applications/devlist/main.cpp
index 41aa6b1..7b451f8 100644
--- a/src/applications/devlist/main.cpp
+++ b/src/applications/devlist/main.cpp
@@ -13,12 +13,14 @@
 #include <iostream>
 #include <iomanip>
 
-const QString kUSBDescriptorPath = tacConfigRoot() + "devicelist.json";
-
 int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 {
 	QCoreApplication a(argc, argv);
 
+	// Built here rather than as a global: tacConfigRoot() reads globals from
+	// QCommonConsole that may not be initialized yet during static init
+	const QString kUSBDescriptorPath = tacConfigRoot() + "devicelist.json";
+
 	USBDescriptors usbDescriptors;
 
 	if (usbDescriptors.load(kUSBDescriptorPath) == true)
